","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-06-19T00:17:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T21:32:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in **Godot Engine v4.7.stable.mono official**\n- Reproducible in **Godot Engine v4.7.dev3.mono.official**\n- Not Reproducible in **Godot Engine v4.7 dev2.mono.official**\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable.mono - macOS Tahoe (26.5.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M1 Max (Apple7) - Apple M1 Max (10 threads) - 32.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nJust got a chance to try out Godot 4.7 and I've found zooming in the 3D Editor view doesn't always work when the Navigation Scheme is set to \"Maya\".\nHere's an example of the issue - \n<img width=\"640\" height=\"556\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbd96014-4770-4d22-825f-f55ea0764c5a\" />\n\nI can't pin down exactly what makes it break but it seems to be more reliable if the cursor is still before you press Option + Right mouse to zoom. It may have something to do with the right click also.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet the Editor Settings/Editors/3D/Navigation Scheme to Maya.\nOpen a 3D view and Option Right Click to zoom on the 3D scene.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe issue can be reproduced in a new empty Godot project.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0